@model Mlcp.Web.Models.LandingViewModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Microsoft licence and cost management";
}

<div class="py-4">
    <h1>See what you own, what you use, and what it costs</h1>

    <p class="lead">
        MLCP connects to your Microsoft Entra tenant and shows your licences, who has them, whether
        they are being used, and &mdash; where your agreement allows it &mdash; what you actually
        pay. Sign in with your work account to start.
    </p>

    @if (Model.PreferredElsewhere is { } preferred)
    {
        <div class="alert alert-info" role="status">
            You chose to use MLCP in @preferred.Name.
            <a href="@preferred.Url">Continue there</a>.
        </div>
    }

    <p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" asp-area="MicrosoftIdentity" asp-controller="Account" asp-action="SignIn">
            Sign in with Microsoft
        </a>
    </p>

    @* ADR-021: data stays in the region chosen here. Signing in on the wrong stack still routes
       an existing organisation to its own region. *@
    <p class="text-muted small">
        Data region: <strong>@Model.Region.Name</strong>.
        @if (Model.Alternatives.Count > 0)
        {
            <span>Use a different region:</span>
            @foreach (var alternative in Model.Alternatives)
            {
                <a class="ms-1" href="@alternative.Url">@alternative.Name</a>
            }
        }
    </p>
</div>

<hr />

<h2 class="h4">Every organisation gets the same starting point</h2>

<p>
    Licences, assignments, renewal dates and waste detection work for every tenant on day one,
    through Microsoft Graph alone. Everything beyond that is a separate unlock you grant, and can
    revoke, at any time.
</p>

<div class="row g-4 mt-1">
    <div class="col-md-3">
        <h3 class="h6">Always included</h3>
        <p class="text-muted small">
            Licences purchased and assigned, unused seats, seats on disabled accounts, overlapping
            products, renewal calendar.
        </p>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-3">
        <h3 class="h6">With usage consent</h3>
        <p class="text-muted small">
            Which services people actually use, who has been inactive for 90 days, Copilot adoption.
        </p>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-3">
        <h3 class="h6">With an Azure role</h3>
        <p class="text-muted small">
            Azure spend by subscription, resource group, resource and tag, with trends and forecast.
        </p>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-3">
        <h3 class="h6">With a billing role</h3>
        <p class="text-muted small">
            The prices you actually pay, invoices, auto-renew status and term end dates.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<h2 class="h4 mt-5">What we are honest about</h2>

<p>
    Not every organisation can see every figure, and that is a limit of what Microsoft exposes
    rather than a limit of the product. If your licences come from a partner, or you are still on
    the older online subscription agreement, no API gives anyone your seat prices. We say so
    plainly, and let you enter the numbers yourself, instead of showing you an empty chart.
</p>

<p class="text-muted">
    We never read your email, files or messages. We cannot buy, assign or remove licences unless
    you separately turn that on. <a asp-action="Privacy">Read the privacy summary</a>.
</p>
